              <p>On a kitchen remodel a few blocks from the borough center, we opened a wall expecting standard framing and found knob-and-tube wiring still live behind the plaster &mdash; original to the house. That's routine for Media's older stock, and it's why we always budget a contingency line for what's behind the walls before we start, rather than after we've already opened them and the homeowner is staring at a change order.</p>
            </div>

